  "story": "Four spikes on one tetrahedron over four pits on its antipode -- the two tetrahedra that together make the cube. Its symmetry is T (order 12, rotations only): alone in this family it has no mirror plane, so a cut through it gives two halves that are genuinely different rather than two copies of one part. That is the point of the piece.",
